{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And the people strove, etc.</b> The meaning is: the strife was that they said to him along the way, ״Give us water.״ But did Moses have water to give them? This was nothing but strife — for if their intention had been to ask that he cry out to HaShem, they should have spoken in the manner they spoke to him (Numbers 21:7) when HaShem sent fiery serpents against them. Or it is possible that they were demanding the water like one who demands a debt from his fellow and says to him, ״Give me what you owe me,״ and they used the language of the plural, yet their words were directed at Moses alone — here they included HaShem. Therefore Moses said to them: <b>Why do you strive with me? Why do you try HaShem?</b> And he said in this order because, in relation to HaShem, they already knew that He is omnipotent; rather, they were testing whether He is among them."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:29:06.530529590Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}